{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155722-dark-eras-lifting-the-veil-integrity","id":1155722,"title":"[Dark Eras] Lifting the Veil & Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-04T07:21:06-07:00","id":1155722,"title":"[Dark Eras] Lifting the Veil & Integrity","content":"I must say I very much liked whole Dark Era of Lifting the Veil - especially the examples of using real world spiritualist organizations for mechanics of CoD 2E Rulebook. But I see this Era miss one of crucial point of it - even mentioned in text of chapter - that in this time 1/5th of society strongly belives in supernatural. People LOOK FOR mediums and spiritists to talk to their dead and other side. It's in starring contrast with Integrity Breaking Points of 'witnessing the supernatural', as people would FLEE from mediums if most of them would be hit by Integrity drops. So what - characters firmly beliving in supernatural should just automatic pass those Breaking Points? Or maybe use the rules from this Hunter the Vigil 2E Playtest that characters are hit on Integrity by witnessing only the first supernatural event of particular kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T08:20:41-07:00","id":1155734,"title":"","content":"Haven't read the DE chapter you're referring to, but I imagine it's like the difference between seeing a bear in a zoo and seeing one while camping in the woods.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to believe in ghosts and visit a medium who claim to channel ghosts. It's another to witness a ghost out of the blue without the sort of expectation and readiness you'd have in a seance, and get haunted with the screaming voices of the dead in your head.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm also reminded of that ancient Chinese idiom/proverb, where a guy who really liked dragons and had portraits and depictions of dragons all over his house fainted when a <i>real </i>dragon showed up to show him gratitude for his 'worship.' In CofD terms, believing in the supernatural and even being fond of it didn't save him from losing a dot of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 11-04-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:05:49-07:00","id":1155745,"title":"","content":"But if Chinese proverb would be true - and Integrity worked like described in CoD Rulebook - people would not RETURN to medium and spiritists for more. The Era itself points that Queen Victoria become OBSESSED with talking to Prince Albert after his death. If Integrity would hit her on each seanse she organized as CoD Rulebook assumed, she would not be one of strongest rulers of Great Britain in it's whole history, with her Integrity dropping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:14:18-07:00","id":1155746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155722-dark-eras-lifting-the-veil-integrity#post1155722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People LOOK FOR mediums and spiritists to talk to their dead and other side. It's in starring contrast with Integrity Breaking Points of 'witnessing the supernatural', as people would FLEE from mediums if most of them would be hit by Integrity drops.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never taken part in a seance? Those aren't mutually incompatible. At least in my experience real life seances tend to end when one or more of the participants has scared themselves to the point that they can't go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:09:02-07:00","id":1155764,"title":"","content":"The question is to determine what level of exposition constitutes a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Even today IRL, most religious rites presume that some sort of supernatural phenomena is occurring. To give the simplest example, most christian churches present to the faithful a transmutation of wheat and grape into meat and blood. Some of the faithful can swear to you that they really taste meat and blood during the sacrament. On my IRL point of view, the people who sense meat is just induced to this by their belief. But on a CoD game, it could be the people who senses just wheat and wine who are hallucinating things in a subconscious attempt to not pierce the veil. They believe and search for this experience, but they still have something between them and a full supernatural experience to protect their minds.<br /> <br /> You can think of this in this case. Human rituals frequently aren't really necessary for the supernatural to occur in CoD. But they do serve a psychological role by adding meaning and a sense of security to people involved. In a time like this, people look for the supernatural far more, but still under protection of such ritae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 11-04-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:56:21-07:00","id":1155903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155722-dark-eras-lifting-the-veil-integrity?p=1155745#post1155745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if Chinese proverb would be true - and Integrity worked like described in CoD Rulebook - people would not RETURN to medium and spiritists for more. The Era itself points that Queen Victoria become OBSESSED with talking to Prince Albert after his death. If Integrity would hit her on each seanse she organized as CoD Rulebook assumed, she would not be one of strongest rulers of Great Britain in it's whole history, with her Integrity dropping.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that, all those seances and such? Not shocking enough to constitute a breaking point in the first place. Unless the supernatural phenomenon in question is Supernal or Abyssal, I'd say the human psyche has some flexibility in how it registers the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:33:21-08:00","id":1155979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155722-dark-eras-lifting-the-veil-integrity?p=1155745#post1155745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she would not be one of strongest rulers of Great Britain in it's whole history, with her Integrity dropping.</div> </div> </div> </div>She wasn't. Victoria was a constitutional monarch.<br /> <br /> Also bear in mind the era seems to indicate that Victoria is still obsessed with Albert 20 years after his death. That doesn't exactly indicate great integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}